    "job": "Extend the existing report command so I can combine multiple CSV inputs, group by item or category, and optionally filter small totals.\n\nAdd repeatable `--input`, `--group-by item|category`, and `--min-total N`. With no options, keep the current source.csv input, item grouping, and no filter. Combine inputs in the order I supply them, keep each group's first-appearance order, and apply the minimum after aggregation, including totals equal to N. Units, multipliers, totals, and N are integers; signed units are valid.\n\nRequire the item, category, units, and multiplier columns and integer numeric fields. Report invalid input on stderr with exit status 1, and leave an existing report untouched if input validation fails. Use the selected grouping key and total_units as the CSV header. Keep both source data files unchanged.\n\nGenerate the category report from data/source.csv followed by data/returns.csv with a minimum total of 10. Update the tests and README, and verify the resulting CLI. Don't create a Git commit.\n\nLatest request: Add `--format csv|json`, keeping CSV as the default. The downstream consumer now needs JSON for the same report: data/source.csv followed by data/returns.csv, grouped by category, with a minimum total of 10.\n\nWrite JSON as an array of objects with category and integer total_units fields; use item instead of category for item grouping. Preserve group order.\n\nAfter successful validation and generation, leave only the current report.csv or report.json in output and remove the obsolete report output. Preserve any unrelated file. Keep the input data unchanged.\n\nUpdate the tests and README, regenerate the requested JSON report, and report what you checked. Don't create a Git commit.",
